>> title: Scallion Schmear
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: cream cheese, scallion, no-cook, spread, deli
>> counters: Deli
>> aka: scallion cream cheese, schmear, schmeer, shmear, green onion cream cheese, spring onion cream cheese
>> pairs-with: bagels, cream-cheese, chocolate-babka
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> step.1: beat the cream cheese soft
>> step.2: slice the scallions thin
>> step.3: fold them through
>> step.4: chill 1 hr

Beat @cream cheese{1%lb}(450 g, at room temperature) with @heavy cream{2%Tbs} and @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} until it is smooth and takes a peak.

Slice @scallions{6}(white and green both) as thin as you can be bothered to, on a slight angle.

Fold @&(~1)sliced scallions{} through @&(~2)beaten cream cheese{} with @white pepper{1/8%tsp} and @lemon juice{1/2%tsp}, turning rather than stirring so the green stays in streaks.

Chill @&(~1)schmear{} ~chill{1%hr} before it goes on anything, so the onion has time to give itself up to the cheese.
